test.yaml:10:16: this step checks out code from a pull request (github.event.pull_request.head.sha) in a "pull_request_target" workflow and "npm" runs it afterwards. the workflow has a write token and secrets, so whoever controls that code can use them. the environment "staging" of job "staging" has no required reviewers, so no one has to approve the run. run untrusted code in a "pull_request" workflow without secrets, or check out the base branch and only read the pull request as data. the pinned actions/checkout (v4.2.2) predates the protection that refuses the code of a fork pull request here, upgrade to v4.4.0 or later [untrusted-checkout]
test.yaml:20:16: this step checks out code from a pull request (github.event.pull_request.head.sha) in a "pull_request_target" workflow and "npm" runs it afterwards. the workflow has a write token and secrets, so whoever controls that code can use them. the environment "prodution" of job "typo" does not exist in example/environments (GitHub creates it without protection when the job runs), so no one has to approve the run. run untrusted code in a "pull_request" workflow without secrets, or check out the base branch and only read the pull request as data. the pinned actions/checkout (v4.2.2) predates the protection that refuses the code of a fork pull request here, upgrade to v4.4.0 or later [untrusted-checkout]
